{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He said</b> — to His own heart, or to the angels. <b>I will hide My face from them</b> — in the manner of human expression, as in 'and I will hide My eyes from you' (Isaiah 1:15), and the reason is that when they seek Me they will not find Me. <b>I will see what their end shall be</b>: some say, 'I will hide My face from them because I see what they will do in the end.' But the correct interpretation is its plain sense: 'until I see what they will do in their distress' — the words of R. Abraham ibn Ezra. And the meaning of <b>and He said</b> is nothing but the thought and the will before Him to do so, in the manner of <b>and Elohim said</b> in the account of Creation, as I have already explained (Genesis 1:3). And the meaning of <b>My face</b> by way of truth, I have explained (Exodus 3:2; ibid. 20:3). Now, <b>I will hide My face</b> means that I will remove My Shekhinah. And the meaning of <b>I will see what their end shall be</b> is like the meaning of <b>I will go down now and see</b> (Genesis 18:21), which I have already explained. <b>For they are a generation of reversals</b> — they will not stand before Me. <b>Children in whom I have no faith</b> — for they have no guardian and nurturer, and the enlightened will understand. Now, up to this point in this song, Moses sings and speaks in his own voice. But from this verse onward, since Scripture mentioned <b>and HaShem saw and spurned</b>, etc., and <b>and He said: I will hide My face</b>, it is all the words of the honored HaShem: <b>they have provoked Me to jealousy, angered Me</b>, and so the entire song."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:45.680527253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}